---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { chapters, v2Chapters, chapterPreviews } from '../../data/chapters';
import { v2Parts } from '../../data/v2-curriculum';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

---
<Layout title="Learning path">
  <p class="eyebrow">Learn · Curriculum transition</p>
  <h1>Develop the system. Develop how you engineer it.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Explore how executable models, software-driven workflows and AI agents change systems engineering—from an uncertain product idea to useful improvements in operation.</p>
  <section aria-labelledby="reader-preview-title">
    <h2 id="reader-preview-title">Start with Chapter 1</h2>
    <p>The opening chapter is a reader preview of the revised content and dark chapter layout.</p>
    {chapterPreviews.map(chapter => <p><a href={`${base}learn/${chapter.path}/`}><strong>{chapter.title} →</strong></a><br />{chapter.summary}</p>)}
  </section>
  <h2>V2 course structure</h2>
  <p><strong>Planned curriculum.</strong> The full sequence below is planned; available v2 articles are linked separately below. <a href="#published-lessons">Go to the published lessons</a> for working examples.</p>
  <div class="parts">{v2Parts.map(part => <section class="card" id={`part-${part.start}`}><h3>{part.title}</h3><p>{part.message}</p><ol start={part.start}>{part.chapters.map(title => <li>{title}</li>)}</ol></section>)}</div>
  <section class="course-language" aria-labelledby="course-language-title">
    <h3 id="course-language-title">A shared vocabulary from Chapter 1</h3>
    <p>The <a href={`${base}learn/v2/01-new-engineering-paradigm/`}>Chapter 1 preview</a> introduces systems engineering, executable engineering, software-driven workflows and AI-assisted engineering. It explains what AI agents do and distinguishes AI used in engineering from AI in products.</p>
    <p>Chapter 7 will develop agentic engineering through delegated tasks, tool use and evaluation, explaining large language models (LLMs) as part of the underlying technology. Later chapters will apply these terms to models, delivery, physical validation and the engineering environment.</p>
  </section>
  <h2 id="published-v2">Published v2 articles</h2>
  <div class="cards">{v2Chapters.map(chapter => <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">V2 · Chapter {chapter.number}</p><h3><a href={`${base}learn/${chapter.path}/`}>{chapter.title}</a></h3><p>{chapter.summary}</p></article>)}</div>
  <h2 id="published-lessons">Published lessons — original course</h2>
  <p>The original twelve lessons and URLs are preserved during migration. The V0 demonstrator remains intentionally limited to one ideal circular sensor.</p>
  <ol class="current" aria-label="Published lessons">{chapters.map(chapter => <li><h3><a href={`${base}learn/${chapter.path}/`}>{chapter.title}</a></h3><p>{chapter.summary}</p></li>)}</ol>
  <p><a href={`${base}lab/`}>Open the existing lab →</a></p>
</Layout>
<style>
  .parts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,21rem),1fr));gap:1rem;margin-bottom:3rem}
  .parts h3{margin-top:0}
  .parts li{margin:.35rem 0}
  .course-language{margin-bottom:3rem}
  .current{padding-left:1.5rem}
  .current>li{margin:1.5rem 0}
  .current h3{margin:0}
</style>
